                "place_type": null,
                "poll": null,
                "post_type": "quote",
                "quote_count": 1,
                "quoted_status_id": "1905611079058637209",
                "quoted_status_profile_id": "1917731",
                "quoted_status_profile_username": "thehill",
                "reply_count": 10,
                "retweet_count": 5,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Americans don\u2019t want bureaucrats sitting in on their doctor\u2019s appointments, and they don\u2019t want them to determine their treatment plans. Burdensome regulations keeping patients from accessing life-saving treatment, like colonoscopies, is not only inconvenient but life-threatening. \n\nRead more about the Reducing Medically Unnecessary Delays in Care Act that I introduced alongside @RepGregMurphy and @RepKimSchrier from @AshleighFields_ at @theHill.\n\n@RepJohnJoyce @RepMcCormick @RepAndyHarrisMD, @timburchett @RepBrianBabin @RepMMM @RepMikeKennedy",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1743175488,
                "view_count": 2908
            },
            {
                "attached_links_expanded_url": [
                    "https://markgreen.house.gov/2025/3/rep-green-reintroduces-bill-to-protect-patients-from-delays-in-medical-care"
                ],
                "attached_links_url": [
                    "https://t.co/lYgFyUlUJJ"
                ],
                "attached_medias_preview_url": [
                    "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GnI1fWsW4AE7qbc.jpg?name=small"
                ],
                "attached_medias_url": [
                    "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/GnI1fWsW4AE7qbc.jpg"
                ],
                "attached_videos": null,
                "author_id": "1080477288955826176",
                "author_username": "RepMarkGreen",
                "community_notes": null,
                "conversation_id": "1905644768899502399",
                "created_time": "2025-03-28T15:34:52",
                "favorite_count": 32,
                "geo_lat": null,
                "geo_lon": null,
                "id": "1905644768899502399",
                "in_reply_to_post_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_username": null,
                "place_country_code": null,
                "place_country_name": null,
                "place_full_name": null,
                "place_type": null,
                "poll": null,
                "post_type": "post",
                "quote_count": 2,
                "quoted_status_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 6,
                "retweet_count": 7,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "As a survivor of both colon and thyroid cancer, I know how critical it is to start treatment as soon as possible. Prior authorization can be a roadblock that costs lives. Doctors need to be able to make fast, life-saving decisions without a jungle of red tape to cut through. That's why I'm introducing my Reducing Medically Unnecessary Delays in Care Act.\n\nThanks for leading this bill with me @RepGregMurphy and @RepKimSchrier!\n\nThanks for co-sponsoring the bill @RepJohnJoyce, @RepMcCormick, \u200b\u200b@RepAndyHarrisMD, @timburchett, @RepBrianBabin, @RepMMM, and @RepMikeKennedy!\n\nThanks for endorsing the bill @AmerMedicalAssn, @AOAforDOs, @EmergencyDocs, @ACPIMPhysicians, @AAFP, @AmCollegeGastro, @AAOHNS, @AAOS1, @ACOFP, @oncologynursing, @MGMA, @NFCAssocaition, @IAFAccess, @SpecialtyDocs, @AAFPRS, @AANSNeuro, @MohsCollege, @AmerGastroAssn, @ASCRStweets, @ASDSMembers, @ASE360, @ASPS_News, @asrsdocs, @AmerUrological, @CSROAdvocacy, @CNS_Update, @NASSspine, @SIRspecialists, and @SCAI!\n\nRead more here:\nhttps://t.co/lYgFyUlUJJ",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1743176092,
                "view_count": 3928
            },
            {
